          {
            "role": "assistant",
            "content": "My name is NIVORA. I'm your intelligent AI assistant.\n\nWhen people talk about the **TTD temple in Andhra Pradesh**, they are referring to the world-famous **Tirumala Venkateswara Temple** managed by **TTD (Tirumala Tirupati Devasthanams)**. \n\nHere is everything you need to know about it:\n\n### 1. What is TTD?\n* **TTD** stands for **Tirumala Tirupati Devasthanams**. It is an independent trust/board that officially manages the administration, finances, security, and rituals of the Sri Venkateswara Temple, as well as several other temples in the region. \n\n### 2. The Temple (Tirumala Venkateswara Temple)\n* **Location:** It is situated in the hill town of **Tirumala**, near Tirupati in the Chittoor district of **Andhra Pradesh**.\n* **The Deity:** The presiding deity is **Lord Venkateswara** (also known as Lord Balaji or Govinda), an incarnation of Lord Vishnu. \n* **Significance:** It is widely considered the **richest Hindu temple in the world** in terms of wealth received (donations) and daily visitor turnout. Millions of devotees visit the temple every year.\n\n### 3. Key Highlights & Traditions\n* **The Seven Hills:** The temple sits atop the seventh peak (Venkatachala) of the Seshachalam Hills, which is why the deity is often called the \"Lord of the Seven Hills.\"\n* **Tirupati Laddu:** The temple is famous worldwide for its holy prasadam, the **Srivari Laddu**, which has a GI (Geographical Indication) tag, meaning authentic laddus can only be made here.\n* **Tonsuring (Kailoo / Mundan):** Millions of devotees shave their hair off as an offering of devotion and surrender of ego to the Lord.\n* **Hundi (Donation Box):** Devotees drop cash, gold, and jewelry into the massive Hundi as offerings.\n\n### 4. Planning a Visit\n* **Darshan Types:** There are various ways to get darshan (glimpse of the deity), including *Sarva Darshan* (free/general queue, which can take many hours), *Special Entry Darshan (₹300)*, and VIP breaks. Booking online via the official TTD website (`tirupatibalaji.ap.gov.in`) in advance is mandatory for special tickets.\n* **Strict Rules:** There is a strict dress code (traditional clothing like dhoti/kurta for men and sarees/salwar kameez for women), and mobile phones, cameras, and leather items are strictly prohibited inside the temple complex.\n\nAre you planning a trip there, Bunny, or did you want to know about booking tickets or history? Let me know!",
