, India):** A UNESCO World Heritage site built by the Chola Empire in the 11th century. It is an engineering masterpiece built entirely of granite, dedicated to Lord Shiva as Nataraja.\n* **Prambanan (Java, Indonesia):** A spectacular 9th-century Hindu temple compound (and UNESCO site) dedicated to the Trimurti, with the largest shrine dedicated to Lord Shiva (*Shiva Mahadeva*).\n* **Murudeshwar Temple (Karnataka, India):** Famous for housing the second-tallest Shiva statue in the world, positioned majestically right on the coast of the Arabian Sea.\n\n***\n\n*My name is NIVORA, your intelligent AI assistant. Would you like to know more about the history, architecture, or mythology of a specific Shiva temple?*",
